{{!--
    Features tab (#7): the ship's embedded `feature` items, rendered through the exact same
    row/fieldset partials as the Inventory tab (`partials/inventory-item.hbs` /
    `partials/inventory-fieldset-items.hbs`).

    That sharing is what the character sheet does too: daggerheart's own
    `templates/sheets/actors/character/features.hbs` renders its feature list through
    `daggerheart.inventory-items` -> `daggerheart.inventory-item`, the same pair its Inventory tab
    uses - so a feature row on a ship gets the same portrait/name/tags/description-expand/controls
    treatment as one on a character, for free. `.features-sections` is the character sheet's own
    container class for that tab (its CSS *is* `.character`-scoped there, so the layout is copied
    by value into `main.scss`, same as `.items-section` was for #6).

    The character sheet splits features into several sections (class/subclass/ancestry/community
    granters, off `system.sheetLists`); a ship has none of those concepts (CONTEXT.md: no
    domains/loadout, class/subclass, ancestry/community), so this is a single section - the same
    shape daggerheart's own generic `templates/sheets/global/tabs/tab-features.hbs` uses for
    non-character actors.

    No equip toggle or quantity input on a feature row, matching the character sheet.
--}}
<section class="tab {{tab.id}} {{tab.cssClass}} spaceship-features" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}">
    <div class="features-sections">
        {{> "dhscifi.inventory-items"
            title="DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Features.title"
            createType="feature"
            collection=features
        }}
    </div>
</section>
